    "t": "Quickstart: Send Your First AI Message in 5 Minutes",
    "g": "Get Started",
    "u": "quickstart.html",
    "d": "Install Nexora on Android, connect your first AI provider with your API key, choose a model, and send your first message in under five minutes.",
    "x": " This guide gets you from zero to your first AI conversation as quickly as possible. You need an Android device, a copy of Nexora installed, and an API key from at least one AI provider. If you do not have an API key yet, sign up with your chosen provider first — links are included in the steps below. Download and Install Nexora Install Nexora on your Android device from the project's GitHub Releases page. Nexora Releases (GitHub) Download the latest APK from the project's GitHub Releases page. Once installation is complete, open Nexora from your home screen or app drawer. Open Settings and Add a Provider Nexora needs at least one AI provider before you can chat. Navigate to the provider settings now. Tap the Settings icon (gear) at the bottom of the sidebar. Select Provider Settings from the settings menu. Many providers are pre-configured — if yours is listed, just tap it and enter your API key. If not, tap the button in the top-right corner to create a new provider. OpenAI Google Gemini Anthropic Claude The most widely used API format. Enter the base URL and API key from your provider to complete the setup. OpenAI has two API versions. Chat Completions is the default in Nexora and is the most popular format supported by the vast majority of providers. The newer Responses API is what OpenAI itself now prioritizes — if you are using the official OpenAI API or a relay that mirrors GPT models, switching to the Responses API is recommended. Tap Use Responses API to enable it. Google's own API format, used exclusively for Google Gemini models. The second most widely adopted API format after OpenAI. Used by Claude and a number of other models as well. Enter Your API Key Paste your API key into the API Key field for the provider you selected. If you are using an unofficial relay that is not built into Nexora, you will also need to set the provider's Base URL when creating a new provider. Treat your API key like a password. Do not share it, and do not paste it into untrusted apps. Nexora stores your key locally on your device and never sends it to Nexora's servers — it goes directly to your chosen provider. After pasting your key, tap Save or Confirm to store the provider configuration. Add Models After configuring a provider, scroll to the Models section at the bottom of the provider screen and tap it. Most providers support fetching the model list automatically — tap the expand button to load the list, then select the models you want to use. To remove a model "
