    "t": "AI Providers — Connect to Your Preferred AI Services",
    "g": "Providers",
    "u": "providers/overview.html",
    "d": "Learn how to add, configure, and switch between multiple AI providers in Nexora, including OpenAI, Google Gemini, Anthropic Claude, and custom endpoints.",
    "x": " Nexora lets you connect to multiple AI services at the same time, so you can pick the right model for every conversation without leaving the app. Each connection you configure is called a provider — it stores the API key, base URL, and any additional options needed to talk to a specific AI service. You can add as many providers as you like, enable or disable them individually, and switch between their models directly from the chat screen. Supported provider types Nexora ships with first-class support for three provider types and a flexible custom option that works with any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. OpenAI Connect to OpenAI's API — including GPT-4o, o-series reasoning models, and the Responses API — or any service that mirrors the Chat Completions endpoint. Google Gemini Access Gemini models directly through the Google AI API, or use Vertex AI with a service account for enterprise deployments. Anthropic Claude Chat with Claude models via the Anthropic API, with optional prompt caching to reduce latency and cost on long conversations. Custom / OpenAI-compatible Point Nexora at OpenRouter, a local Ollama instance, a self-hosted proxy, or any other service that speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions protocol. Add your first provider Open Settings Tap the Settings icon in the bottom navigation bar to open the settings screen. Go to Providers Select Providers from the settings list to see all configured providers. Add a provider Tap Add Provider , choose a provider type, fill in your API key and any other required fields, then save. Add models Inside the provider detail screen, add the model IDs you want to use. Each model appears in the model picker when you start or switch a conversation. Manage multiple providers You can configure as many providers as you need. Use the toggle on each provider card to enable or disable it without deleting your settings. Disabled providers and their models are hidden from the model picker. If you want to compare responses from different providers, add each one separately and switch models between conversations — no re-entering credentials required. Share provider configs with QR codes Every provider detail screen has a Share button that encodes your provider configuration (API key, base URL, and settings — without any added models) into a QR code. Another Nexora user can scan that QR code to import the same provider setup instantly. You can also copy the encoded string and send it over any messaging app. The QR code and share st"
