    "t": "Google Gemini Provider — Set Up Gemini and Vertex AI",
    "g": "Providers",
    "u": "providers/google.html",
    "d": "Connect Nexora to Google's Gemini models using the Gemini API or Vertex AI with a service account for enterprise and private cloud deployments.",
    "x": " The Google provider type connects Nexora to Google's generative AI platform. You can use either the public Gemini API — the quickest option for personal use — or Vertex AI with a Google Cloud service account for enterprise or private-cloud deployments. Both paths support the full range of Gemini models including Gemini 2.5 Pro and Gemini 2.5 Flash. Add a Google provider Open provider settings Go to Settings → Providers and tap Add Provider . Choose Google Select Google from the provider type list. Enter your API key Paste your Gemini API key into the API Key field. You can create a free key at aistudio.google.com/app/apikey . Leave this field empty if you are using a Vertex AI service account instead. Confirm the base URL The base URL defaults to https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta . Leave it unchanged for the standard Gemini API. Add Gemini models Tap Add Model , enter the model ID (for example gemini-2.5-pro or gemini-2.5-flash ), set its display name and capabilities, then save. Save Tap Save to apply your changes. Configuration reference Core fields apiKey string required Your Gemini API key from Google AI Studio. Required when Vertex AI is disabled. If you are authenticating via a Vertex AI service account, leave this blank and fill in the service account fields instead. baseUrl string default: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta The root URL of the Google generative language API. Change this only if you are routing requests through a custom proxy. Vertex AI Enable Vertex AI to route requests through your Google Cloud project instead of the public Gemini API. Vertex AI gives you VPC-SC controls, data-residency guarantees, and enterprise SLAs. vertexAI boolean default: false Switch from the public Gemini API to Google Cloud Vertex AI. When enabled, you must also configure the service account fields below. useServiceAccount boolean default: false Authenticate to Vertex AI using a Google Cloud service account rather than a simple API key. Requires the four service account fields below. privateKey string The PEM-encoded private key from your service account JSON file. Copy the value of the private_key field, including the -----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY----- and -----END PRIVATE KEY----- delimiters. Only required when Use Service Account is enabled. serviceAccountEmail string The client_email value from your service account JSON file (for example my-sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com ). Only required when Use Service Account is enable"
